# Build context exclusions for the web image, whose context is the repository root
# (docs/TASKS.md T32).
#
# The first entry is the one that matters. `apps/web/Dockerfile` does `COPY apps/web ./`, and
# apps/web/.env.local holds a real Auth0 client secret on a developer's machine. Without this
# file a local `docker build` bakes that secret into an image layer — where it survives every
# later COPY, is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and would be pushed to ECR.
#
# CI could never have caught it: a fresh checkout has no .env.local, so the pipeline is green
# and only the developer's own build is poisoned. Found by reading the context, not by a test.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Nothing that is rebuilt inside the image should be shipped into it — and node_modules built on
# a macOS host would quietly break a linux image if it survived the copy.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/target
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Infrastructure state: .tfstate contains the generated database password in plain text.
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
!**/*.tfvars.example

# Test and tooling output.
tests/e2e/test-results
tests/e2e/playwright-report
tests/e2e/blob-report
evals/reports/*.json
evals/reports/*.md

# Not needed to build anything, and .git is large.
.git
.github
docs
benchmarks
**/.DS_Store
